decoder.js and decoder.wasm are the FFmpeg-based wasm decoder built from
the source in dev/decoder/ (its ReadMe documents the build and the changes
over the upstream https://github.com/chandler-stimson/decoder.js that this
extension is derived from).

A GitHub workflow (.github/workflows/build-decoder.yml) rebuilds them on
changes to that directory.

The batch entry point keeps the 0.1.2 contract (worker.js feeds it through
the emscripten file system); the incremental streaming API
(decoder_open / decoder_pull / decoder_seek / decoder_close) is consumed
by worker.js so that a large input never has to be read as a whole.
